# Upstream: giac 2.1.0 usual.cc sqrt, asinasln, asinhasln. (1) sqrt of a _CPLX with MPFR parts (Digits > 14) went to the exact-complex path, which returns sqrt(re) when is_zero(im): for an MPFR part is_zero compares its double with epsilon (1e-12), so an imaginary part of 1e-20 was 0 at any Digits. sqrt(1.0-1e-20*i) at Digits 60 gave 1 (right 1-5e-21*i), sqrt(-1.0-1e-20*i) gave +i (right 5e-21-i, the other side of the cut); asin and acos (sqrt(1-x^2) as sqrt(1-x)*sqrt(1+x)) then gave asin(1e-20*i) = (1e-20+5e-41)*i at every Digits and asin(0.5+1e-20*i) an imaginary part of 8.66e-21 (right 1.1547e-20). Now only an exact 0 imaginary part is 0, and the root is t+i*b/(2t), t = sqrt((|z|+a)/2), for a >= 0, |b|/(2t)+sign(b)*i*t, t = sqrt((|z|-a)/2), for a < 0, with no cancellation on either side. (2) The ln forms of asin and asinh take the ln of 1+O(x), so for a small complex MPFR x they lost about -log2|x| bits in both parts (asin(1e-20*i) at Digits 30: 10 right digits and a real part of 1e-41 where it is 0). Now such an x (both parts MPFR or exactly 0, the larger below 1/4) is taken at its precision plus the bits lost plus 16, and the result rounded back; when x^2 is below the rounding the result is x.
